# Rule catalog — the tool's own data, not user policy (spec 0004).
#
# Unlike every other file in config/, this is shipped and NOT meant to be
# user-edited: a user who can rewrite severity or remediation text can make a
# finding say the opposite of what the check found. Users influence findings
# through additive, visible suppression (agent-rules, spec 0003), never by
# rewriting this table.
#
# Format, pipe-delimited so load_list's comment/blank stripping applies as-is:
#
#   id | severity | title | remediation | citation
#
# - id         <domain>.<rule>, lowercase, hyphen-within-part, dot-between.
# - severity   error | warning | info. Maps to log level: error->err,
#              warning->warn, info->sec. Separate from --fail-on, which counts
#              log levels, not severities.
# - title      short human label, stable across message rewording.
# - remediation what to do about it. Never empty: use the em dash placeholder
#              when there is no sensible value, so a truncated row is detectable.
# - citation   short label pointing at the threat model layer (SECURITY.md),
#              not a URL — labels read in a terminal and do not rot.
#
# This file is DATA. It is parsed, never sourced. Remediation text may contain
# ${VAR}, >>, or backticks as literal prose; they are printed, never evaluated.

# ── brew: Homebrew origin, taps, doctor, deprecated formulae ──────────────────
brew.untrusted-tap | error | Untrusted Homebrew tap | brew untap it, or add it to allowed-taps | SECURITY.md Layer 3
brew.remote-tampered | error | Homebrew remote origin is not the official source | Reset the origin to the official Homebrew remote before updating | SECURITY.md Layer 3
brew.doctor | info | brew doctor reported warnings | Review brew doctor output; most warnings are informational | —
brew.deprecated-formula | info | Deprecated or orphaned formula installed | Migrate to the maintained replacement or uninstall it | —

# ── system: SIP, Gatekeeper, PATH permissions ────────────────────────────────
system.sip-disabled | error | System Integrity Protection is disabled | Re-enable SIP from Recovery: csrutil enable | SECURITY.md Layer 3
system.gatekeeper-disabled | error | Gatekeeper is disabled | Re-enable Gatekeeper: sudo spctl --master-enable | SECURITY.md Layer 3
system.path-world-writable | error | World-writable directory on PATH | Remove write for other on the directory, or drop it from PATH | SECURITY.md Layer 3

# ── boot: kexts, SSV, LaunchDaemons, firmware, FileVault ──────────────────────
boot.non-apple-kext | warning | Non-Apple kernel extension loaded | Confirm the kext is expected; unload and remove if not | SECURITY.md Layer 3
boot.ssv-missing | warning | Signed System Volume snapshot not sealed | Verify the system volume is on a sealed snapshot; reinstall macOS if not | SECURITY.md Layer 3
boot.new-launchdaemon | warning | New LaunchDaemon since last baseline | Confirm the daemon is expected before trusting it | SECURITY.md Layer 3
boot.firmware-pending | info | Firmware update pending | Install the pending macOS update to apply firmware; needs a restart | —
boot.filevault-disabled | warning | FileVault disk encryption is disabled | Enable FileVault in System Settings > Privacy & Security | SECURITY.md Layer 3

# ── npm: global updates, audit, provenance signatures ─────────────────────────
npm.audit | warning | npm audit reported vulnerabilities | Review npm audit and update the affected package to a fixed version | SECURITY.md Layer 2
npm.provenance-unverified | warning | npm package lacks a verified provenance signature | Prefer a version published with provenance, or pin the current one deliberately | SECURITY.md Layer 2

# ── sha: binary SHA recording and drift ───────────────────────────────────────
sha.unexplained-change | warning | Binary SHA changed without a corresponding update | Investigate why the binary changed; a silent change is the alarm | SECURITY.md Layer 4

# ── provenance: Sigstore, GitHub attestations, code signatures ────────────────
provenance.unverified | warning | Provenance attestation could not be verified | Confirm the artifact source; a failed attestation is a supply-chain signal | SECURITY.md Layer 2
provenance.codesign-invalid | error | Code signature verification failed | Do not trust the binary; reinstall from the official source | SECURITY.md Layer 2

# ── vuln: grype, govulncheck, cargo audit, pip-audit ──────────────────────────
vuln.grype | warning | grype reported vulnerabilities in the SBOM | Review the grype report and update affected components | SECURITY.md Layer 4
vuln.govulncheck | warning | govulncheck reported Go vulnerabilities | Update the affected Go module to a patched version | SECURITY.md Layer 4
vuln.cargo-audit | warning | cargo audit reported Rust vulnerabilities | Update the affected crate to a patched version | SECURITY.md Layer 4
vuln.pip-audit | warning | pip-audit reported Python vulnerabilities | Update the affected package to a patched version | SECURITY.md Layer 4

# ── tool: the tool's own failures ─────────────────────────────────────────────
tool.missing-dependency | warning | An optional dependency for a check is missing | Install the named tool to enable this check, or ignore if intentional | —
tool.unparseable-config | warning | A config file could not be parsed | Fix the malformed line; the check ran without its configured input | —
